They applied a **hotfix to the batcher and KV cache settings** on the us-west-2 inference prod cluster: they **reduced the continuous batcher `max_batch_size` to 32**, **tightened `max_wait_ms` to 6**, and **enabled KV cache soft eviction** with **`max_entries` capped at 250,000**.

The exact patch was:

```json
{
  "continuous_batcher": {
    "max_batch_size": 32,
    "max_wait_ms": 6
  },
  "kv_cache": {
    "soft_eviction": true,
    "max_entries": 250000
  }
}
```

They also added a **temporary routing rule** to send requests with **`seq_len >= 2048`** to a **dedicated long-request pool**, to avoid mixing long and short requests in the same batcher.

The hotfix was **a mutex/lock around parameter writes in the batching path** so concurrent requests couldn’t interleave their argument buffers. Specifically, they added this in `serving/runtime/batcher.cc`:

```cpp
std::scoped_lock lock(params_write_mutex);
// preserve param append order per-request
```

The intent was to **serialize param-buffer appends per request** and stop swapped/dropped function arguments caused by shared batching-slot races.
